# onnxruntime-node (narration, through kokoro-js) downloads a CUDA build from GitHub in its postinstall unless
# told to skip it. When that download fails, npm drops kokoro-js’s whole optional subtree and still exits 0, and the
# typecheck then fails. Narration runs on the CPU, so the CUDA build is never needed (tests/npmrc.test.mjs).
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
